// Exception subclass hierarchy.  Each class is an empty-body declaration
// whose only effect is to install a derived proto under Exception (or under
// another error subclass for two-level hierarchies).  No method bodies —
// they all inherit Exception.new + Exception.raise from the parent proto
// chain, and isA-style dispatch routes via the proto-walk in catch.
//
// At v1.0, typed catch (`catch (TypeError e)`) is not yet syntax — the
// generic `catch (e)` form binds the raised UObject directly, and
// e.message resolves through the proto chain to the Exception locals.
// User code that wants per-class branching uses .isA-equivalent host
// predicates, deferred to v1.x.

class TypeError     : public Exception {} |
class ArityError    : public Exception {} |
class LookupError   : public Exception {} |
class KeyError      : public LookupError {} |
class IndexError    : public LookupError {} |
class RangeError    : public Exception {} |
class DivByZero     : public Exception {} |
class IOError       : public Exception {} |
class CapacityError : public Exception {} |
